 "name": "Minimal medium (in silico simulation medium for iAF692) (PMC1681478)",
 "category": "laboratory",
 "organism_scope": "Methanosarcina barkeri",
 "aerobic": false,
 "description": "Minimal medium (in silico simulation medium for iAF692) — a minimal medium extracted from Feist et al. (2006). Mapped to BiGG from the paper's stated composition.",
 "namespace": "bigg",
 "provenance": {
  "source_type": "literature",
  "citation": "Feist et al. Modeling methanogenesis with a genome-scale metabolic reconstruction of Methanosarcina barkeri. Molecular Systems Biology (2006). DOI: 10.1038/msb4100046. [PMC1681478]",
  "doi": "10.1038/msb4100046",
  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1681478/",
  "notes": "Extracted from the primary paper (snippet: 16 mmol methanol gDW−1 h−1 and 8 mmol acetate gDW−1 h−1 (Elferink et al, 1994), 41 mmol H2 gDW−1 h−1 (Smith and Mah, 1978) (the amount of CO2 was not constrained) and 5 mmol pyruvate gDW−1 h−1 (Bock e). Component names mapped to BiGG (see mapping_confidence); presence-based bounds unless the paper gave exchange bounds; concentration_mM where units allowed. Extraction confidence: medium.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "verification_evidence": "Beyond the primary source (methanol, acetate, CO2 or pyruvate), two additional carbon-containing compounds were needed to generate the metabolites present in the BOF: p-aminobenzoic acid (pABA) and nicotinic acid... In addition to carbon-containing compounds, the required compounds are metals, phosphate, sulfur and nitrogen. [uptake rates:] 16 mmol methanol gDW-1 h-1 and 8 mmol acetate gDW-1 h-1, ",
  "verification_confidence": "medium",
